Square hollow sections (SHS) manufactured from Strenx®700MC high-strength steel and supplied by SSAB Special Steels (Sweden) were used as base metal (BM). Chemical composition and experimentally determined mechanical properties of the base metal and filler wires are summarized in Tables  1  and  2 , respectively. Weldability was assessed through the carbon equivalent, which correlates chemical composition with hardenability and susceptibility to brittle microstructures. The carbon equivalent was calculated using the widely known International Institute of Welding (IIW) formula given by Eq. ( 1 ). Owing to the low carbon content and limited hardenability of Strenx®700MC steel, the material is not prone to hydrogen-induced cold cracking; therefore, no preheating or post-weld heat treatment was applied [ 13 ].
